# Sizing a heat pump against a design-day cold snap.
#
# Every input is a range, because every one of them really is: the fabric
# performance of an existing house is not a number anybody knows to three
# significant figures.
#
#   plimsoll examples/heat-pump.plim --svg region.svg

given floor_area      = 180 .. 195 [m^2]
given heat_loss_coeff = 0.9 .. 1.4 [W/m^2/K]   # whole envelope, per kelvin
given indoor_target   = 294.15 [K]             # 21 degrees C
given outdoor_design  = 265.15 [K]             # -8 degrees C
given cop             = 2.4 .. 3.2             # seasonal, at this flow temperature

# Kelvin minus kelvin is kelvin, and the dimension checker knows it.
delta_t     = indoor_target - outdoor_design
heat_demand = floor_area * heat_loss_coeff * delta_t

electrical_input = heat_demand / cop

# The available circuit will not carry more than this. Watch what the limit
# implies about the fabric: heat_loss_coeff can no longer reach its stated 1.4.
electrical_input <= 2.2 [kW]

plot heat_loss_coeff, electrical_input
